From: Md Sadre Alam <md.alam@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 06:43:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mtd: spinand: winbond: add support for W25N01KW

Upstream entry for the Winbond W25N01KW (JEDEC 0xef 0xbe 0x21),
which some Xiaomi BE3600 2.5G (RD15) batches use instead of the
GigaDevice part the original port was tested with. The W25N01KW
shares geometry, OOB layout and ECC status handling with W25N01KV;
QPIC-SNAND supports only 4-bit or 8-bit ECC, hence the 4-bit request.

Signed-off-by: Md Sadre Alam <md.alam@oss.qualcomm.com>

--- a/drivers/mtd/nand/spi/winbond.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/nand/spi/winbond.c
@@ -526,6 +526,15 @@
 					      &update_cache_variants),
 		     0,
 		     SPINAND_ECCINFO(&w25n02kv_ooblayout, w25n02kv_ecc_get_status)),
+	SPINAND_INFO("W25N01KW", /* 1.8V */
+		     SPINAND_ID(SPINAND_READID_METHOD_OPCODE_DUMMY, 0xbe, 0x21),
+		     NAND_MEMORG(1, 2048, 64, 64, 1024, 20, 1, 1, 1),
+		     NAND_ECCREQ(4, 512),
+		     SPINAND_INFO_OP_VARIANTS(&read_cache_variants,
+					      &write_cache_variants,
+					      &update_cache_variants),
+		     SPINAND_HAS_QE_BIT,
+		     SPINAND_ECCINFO(&w25n01kv_ooblayout, w25n02kv_ecc_get_status)),
 	/* 4G-bit densities */
 	SPINAND_INFO("W25N04KV", /* 3.3V */
 		     SPINAND_ID(SPINAND_READID_METHOD_OPCODE_DUMMY, 0xaa, 0x23),
